      "name": "Finite-precision certificate handle",
      "construction": "Use a staged dyadic log-domain Sinkhorn certificate for \\(\\mathsf{CertSinkhorn}(p^{\\mathrm c},q^{\\mathrm c},C,a)\\): allocate the target width across directed rational enclosures for shifted log-sum-exp, exponential, logarithm, and the generalized-KL dual; propagate a per-update enclosure budget through gauge-fixed Sinkhorn iterations; certify a retained-positive-mass floor; normalize retained marginals in rational arithmetic; apply marginal truncation and rank-one deficit repair to obtain exactly feasible \\(\\bar\\pi\\); bound every denominator and encoding length; and combine the iteration count with elementary-function precision costs in one total bit-work ledger. Zero rows and columns are removed before scaling and restored as exact zeros afterward.",
