      "depends_on": [
        "thm:minimax-primal"
      ],
      "status": "to-prove",
      "justification": "The theorem shows that entropy changes exact identification by imposing independence, even when its value bias is uniformly small.",
      "gap": "Franguridi--Liu acknowledge regularization bias but do not characterize exact positive-temperature zero membership.",
      "consumer": "It provides the target audit required before interpreting a regularized UAS attrition or refreshment contour as a sharp identified set."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm:first-order-kl",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "statement": "For each fixed \\(p\\in\\Delta_I\\), \\(q\\in\\Delta_J\\), and \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta\\), including simplex-boundary marginals, the regularized minimizer converges as \\(\\varepsilon\\downarrow0\\) to the unique minimum-\\(H_{p,q}\\) member of \\(A_\\theta(p,q)\\), and \\[D_\\varepsilon(\\theta;p,q)=D_0(\\theta;p,q)+\\varepsilon J(\\theta;p,q)+o(\\varepsilon).\\] If \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_0(p,q)\\), then \\[J(\\theta;p,q)=\\min\\{H_{p,q}(\\pi):\\pi\\in\\Pi(p,q),\\ m_\\theta(\\pi)=0\\}.\\]",
      "free_symbols": [
