    {
      "id": "prop:binary-sanity-reduction",
      "kind": "proposition",
      "statement": "Let \\(I=J=2\\), \\(p=q=(1/2,1/2)\\), \\(d=k=1\\), \\(\\Theta=[0,1]\\), and \\(\\phi_{ij}(\\theta)=\\mathbf1\\{j\\ge i\\}-\\theta\\). Then \\(\\Theta_0(p,q)=[1/2,1]\\), whereas \\(\\{\\theta:D_\\varepsilon(\\theta;p,q)=0\\}=\\{3/4\\}\\) for every \\(\\varepsilon>0\\). With \\(0\\log0=0\\), \\[J(\\theta;p,q)=2(\\theta-1/2)\\log\\{4(\\theta-1/2)\\}+2(1-\\theta)\\log\\{4(1-\\theta)\\},\\qquad \\theta\\in[1/2,1].\\]",
