      "id": "oeq:finite-precision-certificate",
      "kind": "openendedquestion",
      "statement": "Can the finite-precision certificate handle be completed so that, for every rational input satisfying the positive-input and bounded-cost conditions, \\(\\mathsf{CertSinkhorn}(p^{\\mathrm c},q^{\\mathrm c},C,a)=(L,U,\\bar\\pi,\\mathcal T)\\) simultaneously establishes the following seven checkable clauses? First, \\(\\mathcal T\\) contains directed rational lower and upper enclosures for every shifted log-sum-exp, exponential, and logarithm evaluation and for the assembled generalized-KL dual value. Second, a stated accumulated-update budget maps every local enclosure width through every gauge-fixed Sinkhorn update into the final dual enclosure. Third, \\(\\mathcal T\\) proves an explicit retained-positive-mass floor of the form \\(2^{-\\operatorname{poly}(\\ell_{\\mathrm{in}},a^{-1},\\log(1/\\min_{i,j}p_i^{\\mathrm c}q_j^{\\mathrm c}))}\\) for every positive quantity used by scaling and repair. Fourth, exact rational marginal repair returns \\(\\bar\\pi\\in\\Pi(p^{\\mathrm c},q^{\\mathrm c})\\cap\\mathbb Q^{I\\times J}\\). Fifth, every potential, enclosure endpoint, and repaired entry has denominator and encoding length bounded by the same polynomial input ledger. Sixth, the stopping rule has an explicit iteration bound. Seventh, adding iteration, rational-arithmetic, repair, and elementary-function enclosure costs yields total bit work bounded by \\(\\operatorname{poly}(\\ell_{\\mathrm{in}},a^{-1},\\log(1/\\min_{i,j}p_i^{\\mathrm c}q_j^{\\mathrm c}))\\) for fixed \\(I\\), \\(J\\), and \\(R_{\\max}\\), while the returned endpoints satisfy \\[L\\le v_0(C;p^{\\mathrm c},q^{\\mathrm c})\\le U,\\qquad U-L\\le a.\\]",
