        "def:finite-precision-handle",
        "lem:original-value-envelope"
      ],
      "status": "to-prove",
      "justification": "The seven clauses define a checkable finite-precision implementation question, but they do not constitute a field-tier kernel unless a Sinkhorn-specific resource advantage over exact rational minimum-cost flow is also established.",
      "gap": "Orlin's exact minimum-cost-flow algorithm applies to rational two-marginal transport and returns an exact rational primal--dual optimum, hence a zero-width independently checkable certificate. The stated fixed-dimensional finite-width Sinkhorn certificate has no proved asymptotic, parallel, or amortized repeated-query advantage over that baseline.",
      "consumer": "The certificate lets partial-identification software report a finite union of parameter cells whose inclusion decisions can be verified without trusting floating-point convergence flags."
