  "novelty_justification": "{\"claim_boundary\":\"Generic minimax, fixed-instance entropy selection, transport stability, and criterion-set inversion are supporting mathematics. Boundary-valid zero collapse is a population-target diagnostic. None can substitute for a Sinkhorn-specific computational separation.\",\"closest_results\":\"The decisive comparator is Orlin's strongly polynomial exact minimum-cost-flow algorithm. Rational two-marginal transport admits exact rational primal and dual optima whose equality is a zero-width independently checkable certificate. Altschuler--Weed--Rigollet and Lemma 10, Proposition 13, and Theorem 4 of van Apeldoorn et al. remain the closest Sinkhorn and finite-precision scaling references; Franguridi--Liu is the closest econometric reference.\",\"strict_gap\":\"No field-tier strict gap is established under the current assumptions. A viable replacement would require an explicit variable-dimension family and a proved near-linear, parallel, or amortized repeated-query resource separation while preserving outward original-value bounds after transcendental rounding and exact rational repair.\",\"why_not_subsumed\":\"The proposed finite-width fixed-dimensional transcript is subsumed as a certification output by exact rational minimum-cost flow, which returns a stronger zero-width certificate. The carried evidence specifies neither the computational model nor the worked family needed to prove a Sinkhorn-specific advantage, so the angle requires a kernel pivot.\"}"
